	{
		"title": "When each side sends one",
		"kind": "text",
		"request": "The client sends one after its ClientHello when it put a non-empty legacy_session_id there — the two together are what 'compatibility mode' means.",
		"request_hex": "",
		"response": "The server sends one straight after its ServerHello, before the first encrypted record, for the same reason.",
		"response_hex": "",
		"note": "Both are optional in both directions. Requiring one — or refusing a second — breaks real clients, so accept any number and require none.",
